 "id": "pipe-saddle-clamp-petg",
 "brief": "A saddle clamp that holds a 25 mm pipe against a wall, PETG on FDM, printed on its side so the layers stack along the pipe (Y). The wall is the plane z = 0 and the pipe lies on it along Y (its centre at x = 0, z = 12.5). The clamp is 16 mm wide (y = -8 to 8) and stays inside x = -32 to 32, z = 0 to 29. Two M4 screws go into the wall at x = -24 and x = +24 through 5 mm thick feet. The pipe can pull 200 N straight off the wall or push 150 N sideways along X. Safety factor 2.5.",
